// LEGAL POSITIONING NOTE — READ BEFORE EDITING:
// Slovakia is a PERMISSION + DUAL-TRACK market, closest in our
// coverage to HUNGARY — not to the Greece/Netherlands prohibition
// tier and not to Switzerland's cantonal patchwork.
// - The School Act (zákon č. 245/2008 Z. z., § 24) provides for
//   INDIVIDUÁLNE VZDELÁVANIE (individual education), granted by the
//   PRINCIPAL of the kmeňová škola (the school where the pupil
//   remains enrolled) — on health grounds, or on the request of the
//   pupil's legal representative.
// - THE OBLIGATIONS ARE REAL AND MUST ALWAYS BE STATED:
//   * The pupil stays enrolled at the kmeňová škola.
//   * KOMISIONÁLNE SKÚŠKY (commission examinations) are sat at that
//     school — in practice each half-year — against the state
//     curriculum, in Slovak. (Pupils granted individual education on
//     HEALTH grounds are exempt from the commission examination and
//     are assessed instead on the teaching pedagogue's periodic
//     written reports — state this distinction accurately.)
//   * The pedagogue providing the education submits written reports
//     on progress to the principal periodically (quarterly in the
//     health-grounds case; the school's own directive sets the
//     rhythm otherwise), and the pedagogical council then grades.
//   * ŠTÁTNA ŠKOLSKÁ INŠPEKCIA (State School Inspection) controls
//     the QUALITY of education under individual education; the
//     kmeňová škola controls the pedagogical and material provision
//     and the child's health protection — and the legal
//     representative is obliged to permit entry for that check.
//   * The principal may REVOKE the permission.
// - QUALIFICATION: the Act refers to a "pedagogický zamestnanec"
//   (pedagogical employee) providing the education, so qualification
//   requirements attach to the teaching person. Do NOT state the
//   precise qualification rule as settled — say requirements apply
//   and are confirmed with the kmeňová škola and the Ministry.
//   CONSEQUENCE: we do NOT claim to be the pedagogue of record.
//   Position Smartious as the ACADEMIC SPINE beside the arrangement,
//   or supplementary beside an ordinary enrolment.
// - LANGUAGE: the state track runs in Slovak, so Slovak-language
//   preparation runs all year in any dual-track plan — the same
//   discipline our Hungarian and Azerbaijani families apply.
// - THE WINDOW: povinná školská dochádzka is TEN YEARS and lasts at
//   most until the end of the school year in which the pupil turns
//   SIXTEEN. Stredná škola beyond that is not compulsory, so the
//   A-Level years fall outside the obligation entirely. Use it
//   prominently — it is the Hungary/Czech wedge again.
// MARKET NOTE: Slovakia produces more cars per head than any country
// on earth. The corridor is the story: Volkswagen Bratislava, Kia in
// Žilina, Stellantis in Trnava, Jaguar Land Rover in Nitra, plus the
// supplier network — and it connects directly to Győr and
// Kecskemét across the Hungarian border, an hour or two away. The
// international-school tier concentrates almost entirely in
// Bratislava (British International School Bratislava, QSI, Cambridge
// International School, Deutsche Schule, Lycée français and peers);
// Košice has limited provision; the rest of the country has
// essentially none. Fees: Bratislava premium tier, quoted locally —
// hedge rather than inventing figures.
// TIMEZONE: CET (UTC+1) / CEST (UTC+2 summer) — 1-2 hours behind
